cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Mechanical Measurements and Metrology Virtual Lab in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Mechanical Measurements and Metrology Virtual Lab: an open virtual laboratory for transducer calibration, strain and force measurement, and dimensional, angular, surface, thread, gear and optical metrology"
abstract: >-
  Browser-based virtual laboratory with 18 experiments: calibration of a pressure
  gauge with a dead-weight tester, of a thermocouple, a Pt100 RTD, an LVDT, a
  strain-gauge load cell and a tachometer; Young's modulus and Poisson's ratio
  with strain gauges; lathe and drill tool dynamometers; micrometer calibration
  with slip gauges; comparator inspection and limit-gauge design; sine bar;
  autocollimator straightness; stylus surface roughness; optical-flat flatness;
  two-wire thread measurement; gear tooth vernier and base tangent span; and the
  toolmaker's microscope. Each experiment has pre-test, theory with narrated
  explainer, operation with safety briefing and interlocked set-up, instrument
  scales read by the student, validation, randomised numericals, post-test and a
  report with uncertainty analysis; plus a metrology handbook with ISO 286, ITS-90
  and IEC 60751 tables and calculators.
authors:
